Trajectory Analysis package from MDynaMix

Version 5.3:  Support for Gromacs .trr and .xtc files included
(contribution be Alexander Mirzoev)

To compile everything:

./setup.sh

All executables can be found in "bin"

Examples (templates) of input files can be found in "inputs"

Modified / new utilities can be compiled using static libraries
libtranal_base.a and libxdrfile.a in "lib",  for example:

gfortran -o rdf-mod rdf-mof.f -Llib -ltranal_base -lxdrfile


New features
-----------------------------------------

for reading .trr / .xtc trajectories, use statement

NFORM = 'TRR'  or NFORM = 'XTC' 

If only a single trajectory file is analysed, use

NFBEG = -1

Then the trajectory file name should correspond exactly to the nname in
FNAME = 

If NFBEG >= 0, it is supposed that trajectory files are numbered.
The name given in parameter FNAME is complemented by a number changing from
NFBEG to NFEND

